%I A400923 #22 Nov 02 2026 20:09:55
%S A400923 1,1,1,2,3,5,8,14,23,40,67,116,196,339,576,997,1701,2942,5034,8708,
%T A400923 14931,25826,44354,76719,131922,228183,392757,679357,1170254,2024215,
%U A400923 3489121,6035299,10408429,18004151,31063270,53732819,92740844,160423448,276969008,479106535
%N A400923 Number of achiral n-carbon alkyl radicals C(n)H(2n+1) ignoring stereoisomers.
%C A400923 A molecule is achiral if it is superposable on its mirror image. This count includes meso compounds, which are achiral despite containing stereogenic centers.
%C A400923 Distinguishing stereoisomers instead yields A005627.
%C A400923 Counting all rooted ternary trees, whether chiral or achiral, yields A000598.
%H A400923 Andrew Howroyd, <a href="/A400923/b400923.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..1000</a>
%H A400923 Casper Asbjørn Eriksen and Daniel Merkle, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.02932">Enumerating Chemical Structures, Stereoisomers, and Stereogenic Units with Analytic Combinatorics</a>, arXiv:2609.02932 [physics.chem-ph], 2026.
%H A400923 Casper Asbjørn Eriksen, <a href="https://gitlab.com/casbjorn/molenum">Python Notebook</a> (0.2.0).
%F A400923 G.f.: A(x) satisfies A(x) = 1 + x*A(x)*B(x^2), where B(x) is the g.f. of A000598. - _Andrew Howroyd_, Oct 26 2026
%o A400923 (PARI) seq(n)=my(g=O(1),u=O(1)); for(n=0, n, g = 1 + x*(g^3 + 3*subst(g,x,x^2)*g + 2*subst(g,x,x^3))/6; u = 1 + x*(u*subst(g,x,x^2)) ); Vec(u) \\ _Andrew Howroyd_, Oct 26 2026
%Y A400923 Cf. A000598, A005627.
%K A400923 nonn,new
%O A400923 0,4
%A A400923 _Casper Asbjørn Eriksen_, Oct 09 2026
